      "remarks": "Generated by grundschutz-worksheets mapping.mjs from a mapping file. Do not edit by hand.\n\nTargets of the BSI mapping not in the catalog, left out (13): BER.5.1.2 (iso27001 8.2); BER.6.8 (iso27001 5.17); BER.6.8 (iso27001 8.5); DET.3.1.13 (iso27001 5.23); GC.6.1.2 (iso27001 5.4); GC.6.1.3 (iso27001 5.1); GC.6.1.3 (iso27001 5.4); GC.6.1.4 (iso27001 5.1); GC.8.1.1 (iso27001 5.2); GC.8.1.1.1 (iso27001 5.4); GC.8.1.4 (iso27001 5.2); PERF.5.1.4 (iso27001 5.35); PERF.7.1 (iso27001 5.1)."
    },
    "provenance": {
      "method": "hybrid",
      "matching-rationale": "semantic",
      "status": "draft",
      "mapping-description": "The ten risk-management measures of Directive (EU) 2022/2555 Art. 21(2) (a) to (j), which § 30 Abs. 2 Nr. 1 to 10 BSIG (NIS2UmsuCG) transposes one to one. Each measure names the ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A controls it corresponds to; the Grundschutz++ targets of those controls come from the BSI's own mapping. Direct targets cover what Annex A lacks. The step from each measure to ISO is a draft written with AI assistance and not yet reviewed by a person. The Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2690, which makes Art. 21(2) concrete for digital infrastructure and digital providers, has a mapping of its own (mappings/src/nis2-ir.json, step to ISO by ENISA). Not covered: the reporting obligations of Art. 23 / § 32 BSIG."
    },
